# Symlinked mirror of .agents/skills/ — commit the source, not the mirror.
# core.symlinks=false on Windows means git walks these as real files,
# which would duplicate every skill in the repo.
#.claude/skills/

# smart-connections' embedding cache. Per-machine, regenerable, and it indexes
# whatever the vault contains — which is why it must not be tracked: a cache of
# the repo's specs and skills inside wiki/ breaks "the vault holds learning
# content only".
#.smart-env/

# The machine-readable health report `check` writes beside the vault. Regenerated on
# every run, so tracking it would dirty the tree on each check.
.wiki-health/

# Context Packs `generate --layer` writes beside the vault. Transient inputs for one run of
# the Note Author; a Pack committed anywhere, and above all into wiki/, would be read as
# content.
.context-packs/

# Review Bundles `generate --review` writes beside the vault. Transient inputs for one run of
# the Correctness Reviewer, like the Packs.
.review-bundles/
